---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import FAQSection from '@components/article/FAQSection.astro';
import RelatedArticles from '@components/article/RelatedArticles.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '@components/article/ComparisonTable.astro';

// Article metadata
const title = '500 Speed Tests Later, Here\'s What Actually Happened';
const description = 'My wife thought I\'d lost it. Two weeks of VPN testing. Worth it.';
const author = 'FloatJet Team';
const authorUrl = '/about';
const pubDate = new Date('2025-11-23');
const readingTime = 4;
const image = 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558494949-ef010cbdcc31?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80';
const imageAlt = 'Network speed testing visualization with data transfer graphics';

// Table of contents headings
const headings = [
  {text: 'Why I Did This', slug: 'introduction', depth: 2},
  {text: 'What I Found', slug: 'speed-results', depth: 2},
  {text: 'The Testing Part', slug: 'methodology', depth: 2},
  {text: 'The VPNs', slug: 'rankings', depth: 2},
  {text: 'Why VPNs Are Slower', slug: 'speed-factors', depth: 2},
  {text: 'Making It Less Slow', slug: 'speed-tips', depth: 2},
  {text: 'Questions', slug: 'faq', depth: 2},
  {text: 'The Point', slug: 'conclusion', depth: 2},
];

// Speed test comparison table
const speedColumns = [
  {key: 'vpn', label: 'VPN', width: '120px'},
  {key: 'download', label: 'Download'},
  {key: 'upload', label: 'Upload'},
  {key: 'ping', label: 'Ping'},
  {key: 'speedLoss', label: 'Speed Loss'},
];

const speedRows = [
  {
    vpn: '<strong>NordVPN</strong>',
    download: '445 Mbps',
    upload: '42 Mbps',
    ping: '24ms',
    speedLoss: '11%'
  },
  {
    vpn: '<strong>ExpressVPN</strong>',
    download: '432 Mbps',
    upload: '40 Mbps',
    ping: '28ms',
    speedLoss: '14%'
  },
  {
    vpn: '<strong>Surfshark</strong>',
    download: '410 Mbps',
    upload: '38 Mbps',
    ping: '31ms',
    speedLoss: '18%'
  },
  {
    vpn: '<strong>CyberGhost</strong>',
    download: '385 Mbps',
    upload: '35 Mbps',
    ping: '35ms',
    speedLoss: '23%'
  },
  {
    vpn: '<strong>ProtonVPN</strong>',
    download: '378 Mbps',
    upload: '34 Mbps',
    ping: '38ms',
    speedLoss: '24%'
  },
  {
    vpn: '<strong>Private Internet Access</strong>',
    download: '365 Mbps',
    upload: '32 Mbps',
    ping: '42ms',
    speedLoss: '27%'
  },
];

// FAQ data
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Slower?',
    answer: '<p>Yes. 10-15%. Won\'t notice.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Fastest protocol?',
    answer: '<p>WireGuard. Just use it.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Distance matter?',
    answer: '<p>Yes. Stay close.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can VPN make things faster?',
    answer: '<p>Sometimes. If your ISP throttles streaming, VPN bypasses it.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Speed I need?',
    answer: '<p>25 Mbps for video calls. 50+ for 4K. Add 15% buffer for VPN.</p>'
  }
];

// Related articles
const relatedArticles = [
  {
    title: 'Best VPNs for Digital Nomads',
    excerpt: 'Complete guide to choosing the right VPN for remote work, with full reviews of top providers.',
    href: '/tools/best-vpn-digital-nomads',
    image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80',
    imageAlt: 'Digital security concept'
  },
  {
    title: 'VPN & Public WiFi Security Guide',
    excerpt: 'How to stay safe on public networks while traveling and working remotely.',
    href: '/blog/vpn-public-wifi-guide',
    image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1563013544-824ae1b704d3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80',
    imageAlt: 'Person working at cafe on laptop'
  },
  {
    title: 'Find Reliable WiFi Anywhere',
    excerpt: 'Tips and tools for finding fast, stable internet connections while traveling.',
    href: '/blog/find-reliable-wifi-anywhere',
    image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1521791136064-7986c2920216?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80',
    imageAlt: 'WiFi signal concept'
  }
];
---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="Security"
    categorySlug="tools/vpn"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">Why I Did This</h2>
  <p>
    "Lightning-fast speeds!"
  </p>
  <p>
    Every VPN website. Every single one. Meaningless words from marketing departments.
  </p>
  <p>
    I got curious. Or obsessed. Two weeks, 500+ speed tests, my wife asking if I was okay. Different
    times, different servers, different continents.
  </p>
  <p>
    The answer? Good VPNs cost you 10-15% speed. Bad ones? Half your bandwidth. Gone.
  </p>

  <!-- Speed Test Results -->
  <h2 id="speed-results">What I Found</h2>
  <p>
    Started with 500 Mbps. Fiber. East Coast.
  </p>

  <ComparisonTable columns={speedColumns} rows={speedRows}/>

  <p>
    NordVPN won. Not dramatically, but every single time. ExpressVPN was steadier—same speed whether
    I connected to New York or Singapore. Some VPNs are fast nearby and garbage far away. Express
    wasn't like that.
  </p>
  <p>
    Surfshark though. Under three bucks. Faster than stuff costing twice as much. That surprised me.
  </p>

  <!-- Testing Methodology -->
  <h2 id="methodology">The Testing Part</h2>
  <p>
    Look, I know "I tested things" means nothing without details.
  </p>
  <p>
    500 Mbps fiber. MacBook. Windows desktop. Speedtest.net and fast.com, averaged together because
    they give different numbers and I wanted to be fair.
  </p>
  <p>
    Morning tests. Afternoon tests. Evening tests. Same day for all VPNs so conditions were equal.
  </p>
  <p>
    New York servers. LA. London. Frankfurt. Singapore.
  </p>
  <p>
    WireGuard protocol everywhere it existed. That part matters more than people realize.
  </p>

  <!-- Fastest VPNs Ranked -->
  <h2 id="rankings">The VPNs</h2>

  <h3>NordVPN</h3>
  <p>
    This is what's running on my laptop right now.
  </p>
  <p>
    Their NordLynx thing? It's WireGuard underneath but somehow faster than other WireGuard
    implementations. I don't know why. Don't care. It works.
  </p>
  <p>
    11% slower. On a Zoom call I literally cannot tell. Streaming? Fine. Uploading a 2GB file to a
    client? Maybe an extra minute. Maybe.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/nordvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Get NordVPN (68% off) &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <h3>ExpressVPN</h3>
  <p>
    14% speed loss but here's the thing—it didn't matter where I connected.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some VPNs: great to nearby servers, terrible to far ones. ExpressVPN was just... consistent.
    Singapore worked like New York worked like London.
  </p>
  <p>
    Costs more though. Noticeably.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/expressvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Try ExpressVPN risk-free &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <h3>Surfshark</h3>
  <p>
    The cheap one that doesn't suck.
  </p>
  <p>
    18% speed loss. Under $3/month. Unlimited devices.
  </p>
  <p>
    I recommended this to my brother-in-law last month. He's on some 100 Mbps plan and streaming
    works fine. For most people this is plenty.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/surfshark" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Get Surfshark (81% off) &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <!-- What Affects VPN Speed -->
  <h2 id="speed-factors">Why VPNs Are Slower</h2>
  <p>
    Extra stop. Your data goes: you → VPN server → wherever it's going. Instead of just... going there.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Distance matters.</strong> Server in your city is fast. Server across an ocean is slow.
    Physics doesn't care about marketing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Crowded servers.</strong> Popular ones get packed. Try a different server in the same
    city. Usually fixes it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Protocol.</strong> WireGuard is fast. OpenVPN is not. If your VPN has WireGuard, use it.
    NordVPN calls it NordLynx. ExpressVPN calls it Lightway. Same concept.
  </p>

  <!-- Tips for Faster Speeds -->
  <h2 id="speed-tips">Making It Less Slow</h2>
  <p>
    Use WireGuard. I keep saying this. It's 2-3x faster than OpenVPN.
  </p>
  <p>
    Stay close. The quick connect button picks nearby servers. Use it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Switch servers. One slow? Try another. Same city even. They're different.
  </p>
  <p>
    Plug in. Ethernet beats WiFi. Always has.
  </p>

  <h3>Oh Also</h3>
  <p>
    Sometimes VPN makes things faster. Sounds backwards but: if your ISP throttles streaming, VPN
    bypasses it. Run a speed test without VPN, then with. If Netflix is faster with VPN on? Your
    ISP is the problem.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <FAQSection faqs={faqs}/>

  <!-- Conclusion -->
  <h2 id="conclusion">The Point</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/nordvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored">NordVPN</a> is fastest. I use it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/expressvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored">ExpressVPN</a> if you need consistency across countries.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/surfshark" rel="nofollow sponsored">Surfshark</a> if budget matters.
  </p>
  <p>
    All have refund windows. Test yourself. My 500 tests don't mean anything if your connection is
    different than mine.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two weeks. My wife definitely thought I'd lost it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Probably worth it though.
  </p>

  <!-- Related Articles -->
  <Fragment slot="full-width">
    <RelatedArticles articles={relatedArticles}/>
  </Fragment>
</ArticleLayout>
